From a9c8c0f3cdf312641b3d8b95d144daa9b4f1b08d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 15:59:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add client ID management with whitelist,
 disable/enable, and REST API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Whitelist table: only allow pre-approved IDs to register when ENABLE_WHITELIST=Y
- Peer disable/enable: use existing status column (0=disabled, 1=active)
- last_online tracking: updated in DB on every successful RegisterPk
- Online status: derived from in-memory last_reg_time (< 30s = online)
- Management REST API on port API_PORT (default: main_port+3, e.g. 21119)
  - GET  /api/peers              — list all peers with online/offline/disabled/last_online
  - POST /api/peers/:id/disable  — disable a peer
  - POST /api/peers/:id/enable   — enable a peer
  - GET  /api/whitelist          — list whitelist
  - POST /api/whitelist          — add ID to whitelist
  - DELETE /api/whitelist/:id    — remove ID from whitelist
- Auth: X-Api-Key header (set via API_KEY env var; empty = no auth)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EvMxReWsyLxKvxRd6ksktn
